1
00:00:01,871 --> 00:00:03,264
[instrumental music]

2
00:00:07,833 --> 00:00:08,791
Hey.

3
00:00:10,662 --> 00:00:13,578
So I'm pulling turf
out of my teeth, right?

4
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:16,973
We're on our own 8 yard line.
Third and 25.

5
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:18,757
The crowd's hollering
for our blood, right?

6
00:00:18,844 --> 00:00:20,455
Hey, Doc.

7
00:00:20,542 --> 00:00:23,066
So I look over at the guys

8
00:00:23,153 --> 00:00:26,156
and I say, "gentlemen..."

9
00:00:26,243 --> 00:00:29,638
I believe we got 'em
right where we want 'em

10
00:00:29,725 --> 00:00:31,944
Hey, I wanna get you guys
another round. Right?

11
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:35,209
Still gotta pay for it,
but I'm gonna get it for you.

12
00:00:35,296 --> 00:00:37,863
- Here you go, Doc.
- Hey, thanks.

13
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:39,996
Hey. Hey. Just booked
a guest spot Thursday.

14
00:00:40,083 --> 00:00:41,432
Oh.

15
00:00:41,519 --> 00:00:43,260
Who's the greatest
agent in the world?

16
00:00:43,347 --> 00:00:44,566
You are, Alex.

17
00:00:44,653 --> 00:00:47,873
Star quarterback to TV star.
Just wait.

18
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:50,485
Good man, Jakey.
And you're my biggest fan,

19
00:00:50,572 --> 00:00:53,009
Say, you and I go
talk some business.

20
00:00:53,096 --> 00:00:54,663
Busy, busy, busy.

21
00:00:54,750 --> 00:00:57,231
[indistinct chattering]

22
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:08,938
[horn blaring]

23
00:01:09,025 --> 00:01:10,983
[man]
Yo, Doc! You're the best!

24
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:12,333
'Hey, how about an autograph?'

25
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:13,899
Alex, you seen the big man?

26
00:01:13,986 --> 00:01:16,206
Got a question about
that fan expo in Florida.

27
00:01:16,293 --> 00:01:18,426
Yeah, he's just leaving.
You might catch him.

28
00:01:18,513 --> 00:01:20,471
- Thanks, man.
- Alright, Steve.

29
00:01:20,558 --> 00:01:22,734
[explosion]

30
00:01:26,564 --> 00:01:29,089
[indistinct chattering]

31
00:01:30,307 --> 00:01:31,874
[man #1]
'Did you see anything?'

32
00:01:31,961 --> 00:01:34,964
[man #2]
'No, stay back!'

33
00:01:35,051 --> 00:01:36,400
Oh, Doc!

34
00:01:40,056 --> 00:01:42,493
[intense music]

35
00:01:43,712 --> 00:01:46,193
[siren blaring]

36
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:50,501
Agent Wainright,
Lisbon's on her way over.

37
00:01:50,588 --> 00:01:51,937
What about Rigsby?

38
00:01:52,024 --> 00:01:54,288
Apparently, doc was killed
with a car bomb.

39
00:01:54,375 --> 00:01:56,333
Rigsby's in San Francisco
for court.

40
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:58,030
Who's Doc?

41
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,207
I thought you knew.
Our victim's Doc Dugan.

42
00:02:01,338 --> 00:02:03,079
You know, the..

43
00:02:03,166 --> 00:02:04,472
Is that football?

44
00:02:04,559 --> 00:02:06,604
Uh... yeah.

45
00:02:06,691 --> 00:02:08,084
Doc Dugan is dead.

46
00:02:08,171 --> 00:02:09,607
And to make matters
more interesting,

47
00:02:09,694 --> 00:02:11,914
one of our witnesses put
the explosion on YouTube.

48
00:02:12,001 --> 00:02:14,134
- It's gone viral.
- Well, welcome to the future.

49
00:02:14,221 --> 00:02:15,570
They promise us jet packs

50
00:02:15,657 --> 00:02:17,920
they give us
compromised investigations.

51
00:02:18,007 --> 00:02:22,359
Look, I'll, I'll take care of
the media. You guys just go..

52
00:02:22,446 --> 00:02:23,404
...solve the case.

53
00:02:24,622 --> 00:02:27,234
[police radio chatter]

54
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:33,196
Traffic on the 5, Cho?

55
00:02:33,283 --> 00:02:35,067
You recognize my footsteps.
That's weird.

56
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,634
Van Pelt saw
someone she knew.

57
00:02:36,721 --> 00:02:38,941
She didn't do the "boss is
here" posture check.

58
00:02:39,028 --> 00:02:41,335
Rigsby's away.
Therefore, Cho.

59
00:02:44,294 --> 00:02:46,688
Agent and manager saw
the whole thing.

60
00:02:46,775 --> 00:02:49,865
Agent and manager
for a sports bar owner.

61
00:02:49,952 --> 00:02:52,563
Well, even you know
who Doc Dugan was.

62
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:54,609
Someone rich and famous
and full of himself,

63
00:02:54,696 --> 00:02:55,914
judging by the ride.

64
00:02:56,001 --> 00:02:57,873
Doc Dugan is
one of two quarterbacks

65
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,701
to throw 50 touchdowns
in a year

66
00:02:59,788 --> 00:03:03,139
and the only one to throw over
3,000 yards in eight seasons.

67
00:03:03,226 --> 00:03:06,098
He's a local boy. Retired two
years ago, opened that bar.

68
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:07,491
Football star.

69
00:03:11,365 --> 00:03:13,193
He ever win the big game?

70
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,281
2003.

71
00:03:16,283 --> 00:03:17,240
Excuse me.

72
00:03:22,289 --> 00:03:25,205
- You're the agent?
- Manager. Steve Penn.

73
00:03:25,292 --> 00:03:27,076
I'm the agent.
I'm Alex Sodko.

74
00:03:27,163 --> 00:03:30,601
Listen, I think I saw somebody
running away after the blast.

75
00:03:30,688 --> 00:03:32,386
I think I saw him, too.

76
00:03:32,473 --> 00:03:34,605
Did Doc have a place
nearby somewhere

77
00:03:34,692 --> 00:03:36,781
where he could be alone?

78
00:03:36,868 --> 00:03:38,043
He's got an office--

79
00:03:38,130 --> 00:03:41,046
Not an office.
A-a privateplace.

80
00:03:41,133 --> 00:03:43,397
There's a studio apartment
down the block.

81
00:03:43,484 --> 00:03:44,963
He used it as a guesthouse.

82
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:46,530
Take me there right now.

83
00:03:46,617 --> 00:03:47,923
Alright. This way.

84
00:03:50,882 --> 00:03:52,319
what's this about?

85
00:03:52,406 --> 00:03:55,322
A victim's private places
tell you a lot about 'em.

86
00:03:55,409 --> 00:03:57,802
I gotta hunch we'll find
a better than average lead.

87
00:03:57,889 --> 00:03:59,282
Like what?

88
00:03:59,369 --> 00:04:01,284
Oh, his championship ring,
for starters.

89
00:04:02,981 --> 00:04:05,332
[intense music]

90
00:04:07,638 --> 00:04:09,249
Doc?

91
00:04:09,336 --> 00:04:10,554
What the hell?

92
00:04:10,641 --> 00:04:12,991
Ah, like I said, the ring
for starters.

93
00:04:14,297 --> 00:04:15,646
And, of course,
there's the..

94
00:04:17,387 --> 00:04:18,519
...better than average.

95
00:04:21,565 --> 00:04:24,264
[theme music]

96
00:04:30,835 --> 00:04:32,750
[horn honks]

97
00:04:32,837 --> 00:04:35,840
[man #1]
'Yo, Doc! Come back!
Hey, how about an autograph?'

98
00:04:35,927 --> 00:04:37,625
[explosion]

99
00:04:37,712 --> 00:04:38,669
ohh!

100
00:04:40,323 --> 00:04:41,455
Oh, poor Jakey.

101
00:04:43,239 --> 00:04:44,762
[sighs]

102
00:04:44,849 --> 00:04:46,286
[Lisbon]
You didn't hear the explosion?

103
00:04:46,373 --> 00:04:48,375
Huh? Yeah, I heard it.
I was busy.

104
00:04:48,462 --> 00:04:49,550
[sighs deeply]

105
00:04:49,637 --> 00:04:50,986
I should be dead.

106
00:04:51,073 --> 00:04:53,423
Somebodyis.
Tell us about Jake.

107
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:56,034
He was Doc's assistant
for the past year or so.

108
00:04:56,121 --> 00:04:57,471
He's a great kid.

109
00:04:57,558 --> 00:05:00,909
I loved that kid.
I-I loved that kid.

110
00:05:00,996 --> 00:05:03,346
I'll never find
another assistant like that.

111
00:05:03,433 --> 00:05:07,045
Why was Jake driving your car
and wearing your jacket?

112
00:05:07,132 --> 00:05:09,134
Oh, I was dodging a subpoena.

113
00:05:09,221 --> 00:05:10,614
Another lawsuit?

114
00:05:11,702 --> 00:05:12,964
You didn't tell us that.

115
00:05:13,051 --> 00:05:15,010
Well, Anna's looking
for more money.

116
00:05:15,097 --> 00:05:17,186
- Who's Anna?
- My ex-wife.

117
00:05:17,273 --> 00:05:19,449
Look, Jake and I look
like each other,

118
00:05:19,536 --> 00:05:22,974
so sometimes I'd have him
go out and cover my trail.

119
00:05:24,672 --> 00:05:25,803
Poor Jake.

120
00:05:25,890 --> 00:05:27,239
[cell phone ringing]

121
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,459
Oh, it's a reporter.

122
00:05:29,546 --> 00:05:31,853
Well, he's about to get
a great scoop.

123
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:33,507
Doc Dugan lives.

124
00:05:33,594 --> 00:05:36,858
Give that, please. Excuse me.
Thank you. Hello.

125
00:05:36,945 --> 00:05:38,686
[Jane]
'Which paper you with?'

126
00:05:38,773 --> 00:05:41,210
This is Patrick Jane
with the CBI.

127
00:05:41,297 --> 00:05:43,473
[Jane]
'California Bureau
Of Investigation.'

128
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,996
Oh, you heard
Doc Dugan's dead?

129
00:05:45,083 --> 00:05:46,607
[inhales]
Yeah.

130
00:05:46,694 --> 00:05:48,173
Uh really, really dead.

131
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:50,175
Wicked witch of the west dead.

132
00:05:50,262 --> 00:05:51,612
[Jane]
'Okay. Alright.'

133
00:05:51,699 --> 00:05:53,614
Thank you. I'm sorry. Bye.

134
00:05:53,701 --> 00:05:54,745
What was that?

135
00:05:54,832 --> 00:05:56,660
- I'm not dead.
- Yes, you are.

136
00:05:56,747 --> 00:05:58,183
Think about it.

137
00:05:58,270 --> 00:05:59,663
The people in this room

138
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:01,926
are the only people that know
he's still alive.

139
00:06:02,013 --> 00:06:04,015
We've never had
a live murder victim before.

140
00:06:04,102 --> 00:06:06,496
- So?
- So embrace it.

141
00:06:06,583 --> 00:06:09,804
How many times during a case we
wished we talk to the victim?

142
00:06:09,891 --> 00:06:11,632
Are you crazy?
What about them?

143
00:06:11,719 --> 00:06:14,461
Well, tell 'em Doc left
and then the bomb went off.

144
00:06:14,548 --> 00:06:18,682
I don't know, Doc. This is, uh,
this is a little out there.

145
00:06:18,769 --> 00:06:20,989
- A little?
- I don't want to play dead.

146
00:06:21,076 --> 00:06:22,643
Do you wanna
catch the killer?

147
00:06:22,730 --> 00:06:24,688
Huh? Do you want
to catch the killer?

148
00:06:24,775 --> 00:06:26,734
Okay, then trust me.

149
00:06:26,821 --> 00:06:29,824
We will run a trick play
they will never see coming.

150
00:06:36,265 --> 00:06:38,223
- Let's do it.
- Splendid.

151
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:41,096
We'll hide you
in a spare office at the CBI.

152
00:06:41,183 --> 00:06:42,924
Won't Wainright
have a problem with that?

153
00:06:43,011 --> 00:06:44,491
Uh, well, we--we won't tell him.

154
00:06:44,578 --> 00:06:46,493
What he doesn't
know won't hurt him.

155
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:49,278
Compile a list of friends and
family for Lisbon to interview?

156
00:06:49,365 --> 00:06:51,454
No. No, what about
Jake's next of kin?

157
00:06:51,541 --> 00:06:53,761
Oh, I-I have to tell
his mother.

158
00:06:53,848 --> 00:06:56,154
[Jane]
'No, no, no.
You stay out of sight.'

159
00:06:56,241 --> 00:06:57,504
What do you say, Lisbon?

160
00:06:57,591 --> 00:06:59,027
Huh? What do you say?

161
00:07:06,164 --> 00:07:12,170
Mrs. Stewart, I know it's a lot
to ask but I'm asking.

162
00:07:12,257 --> 00:07:14,216
Will you let us
make it look like

163
00:07:14,303 --> 00:07:17,262
it was Doc that died in the
explosion and not your son?

164
00:07:21,397 --> 00:07:23,312
If you say no,
we won't do it.

165
00:07:26,010 --> 00:07:29,536
Will it help you catch
my son's killer?

166
00:07:29,623 --> 00:07:32,364
I can't promise you that
but that's our hope.

167
00:07:34,758 --> 00:07:36,499
But first,
I have to ask you

168
00:07:38,675 --> 00:07:40,155
do you think
it was possible

169
00:07:40,242 --> 00:07:42,462
that Jake was
the intended victim?

170
00:07:44,376 --> 00:07:45,334
No.

171
00:07:47,118 --> 00:07:49,860
It's impossible that anyone
would want to hurt my son Jake.

172
00:07:51,906 --> 00:07:54,299
Doc, on the other hand--

173
00:07:54,386 --> 00:07:55,953
He had a lot of enemies.

174
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,041
[sighs]

175
00:07:58,913 --> 00:08:00,828
Let me put it to you
this way.

176
00:08:02,351 --> 00:08:03,744
There are only two people

177
00:08:03,831 --> 00:08:07,182
in the world
who really loved Doc Dugan.

178
00:08:07,269 --> 00:08:09,053
One of them was my son.

179
00:08:11,055 --> 00:08:12,535
The other one was Doc himself.

180
00:08:17,801 --> 00:08:19,237
[sighs]

181
00:08:19,324 --> 00:08:20,412
Two days.

182
00:08:22,327 --> 00:08:23,981
You got two days.

183
00:08:26,201 --> 00:08:28,159
And then I intend
to bury my son.

184
00:08:30,379 --> 00:08:32,512
[intense music]

185
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:37,647
You're the agent
and you're the manager.

186
00:08:37,734 --> 00:08:39,214
There's a difference.

187
00:08:39,301 --> 00:08:40,520
You're the enforcer

188
00:08:40,607 --> 00:08:42,739
and you,
in your jeans and blazer

189
00:08:42,826 --> 00:08:44,785
are the hand holder,
the enabler.

190
00:08:44,872 --> 00:08:47,831
[chuckles]
The enabler. You're pretty good.

191
00:08:47,918 --> 00:08:49,746
Managers are more one-on-one.

192
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:51,661
I've been with Doc
since the beginning.

193
00:08:51,748 --> 00:08:53,054
You played a little ball.

194
00:08:53,141 --> 00:08:57,188
Yeah. Till my knee took me
out. Then I saw Doc,

195
00:08:57,275 --> 00:08:59,974
college kid with one
of the best arms I've ever seen.

196
00:09:00,061 --> 00:09:02,237
I said I'll take
him to the promised land.

197
00:09:02,324 --> 00:09:03,368
Touching story.

198
00:09:04,761 --> 00:09:07,851
You're the mercenary.

199
00:09:07,938 --> 00:09:09,636
I get things done.

200
00:09:09,723 --> 00:09:11,638
It's been two years
since Doc's been out.

201
00:09:11,725 --> 00:09:13,291
It's time for a comeback.

202
00:09:13,378 --> 00:09:15,946
Steve thinks that having a house
full of signed memorabilia

203
00:09:16,033 --> 00:09:17,644
makes for a pension plan.

204
00:09:17,731 --> 00:09:21,604
Meanwhile, I'm out getting him
endorsement deals, TV deals--

205
00:09:21,691 --> 00:09:24,128
And he's modest, too.

206
00:09:24,215 --> 00:09:25,782
I see.

207
00:09:25,869 --> 00:09:28,524
Agent Lisbon will interview
everyone that ever met Doc

208
00:09:28,611 --> 00:09:31,440
so, uh, let's save her
some time.

209
00:09:31,527 --> 00:09:32,572
Who killed him?

210
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:36,010
Nobody would want
to hurt doc.

211
00:09:36,097 --> 00:09:37,751
No. Everybody loved him.

212
00:09:37,838 --> 00:09:41,581
Liars, both of you.
But I suppose it's your job.

213
00:09:41,668 --> 00:09:43,495
Close your eyes.

214
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,062
Just close 'em.

215
00:09:45,149 --> 00:09:47,108
Doc's dead.
Who do you think killed him?

216
00:09:47,195 --> 00:09:50,590
On the count of three,
say who. One, two..

217
00:09:52,374 --> 00:09:53,941
three. Who?

218
00:09:54,028 --> 00:09:55,682
- Marie St. Claire.
- Marie St. Claire?

219
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,947
Yeah, doc's girlfriend.

220
00:10:00,034 --> 00:10:01,209
Can't wait to meet her.

221
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:07,345
- 'Agent Lisbon.'
- Sir.

222
00:10:07,432 --> 00:10:09,957
Doc's agent sent over some
of the threats he'd received.

223
00:10:10,044 --> 00:10:11,785
Some of them jumped out at me.

224
00:10:11,872 --> 00:10:14,439
Uh, "I want to see
Doc taken out back and..."

225
00:10:14,526 --> 00:10:16,485
- Ooh.
- Oh.

226
00:10:16,572 --> 00:10:17,878
"Someone should
rip off his..."

227
00:10:19,706 --> 00:10:20,837
You get the idea.

228
00:10:20,924 --> 00:10:22,883
All signed by "megafan8."

229
00:10:22,970 --> 00:10:25,189
Number 8--
That's Doc's jersey number.

230
00:10:25,276 --> 00:10:27,757
Fan sending hate mail.
I'll get Cho on to it.

231
00:10:27,844 --> 00:10:30,934
Good. Weren't you
just heading upstairs?

232
00:10:31,021 --> 00:10:32,806
No, no. Of course not.

233
00:10:32,893 --> 00:10:35,199
I don't know
what I was thinking.

234
00:10:35,286 --> 00:10:37,245
Make sure you get
enough rest, Agent Lisbon.

235
00:10:37,332 --> 00:10:38,986
- It's good for the brain.
- Yes, sir.

236
00:10:41,510 --> 00:10:43,773
[intense music]

237
00:10:47,298 --> 00:10:51,215
[male commentator on TV]
'An athlete,
a leader, and a champion.'

238
00:10:52,913 --> 00:10:55,480
'The world says good-bye
to one of the greats.'

239
00:10:56,264 --> 00:10:57,395
[knock on door]

240
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:02,662
I haven't been on television
this much since I retired.

241
00:11:02,749 --> 00:11:05,926
Turns out the best day of your
life's the one after you die.

242
00:11:07,318 --> 00:11:09,059
We've just been going
through your list.

243
00:11:11,192 --> 00:11:13,629
The list of people
who might want to kill you.

244
00:11:13,716 --> 00:11:15,457
You left your ex-wife off.

245
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:18,068
What's the big whoop?

246
00:11:18,155 --> 00:11:19,983
Typically,
in a murder investigation

247
00:11:20,070 --> 00:11:23,378
detective likes to decide what
is and is not a big whoop.

248
00:11:23,987 --> 00:11:25,859
Fine.

249
00:11:25,946 --> 00:11:28,296
Name's Anna Favreau.
I have her number.

250
00:11:28,383 --> 00:11:30,037
Alright.

251
00:11:30,124 --> 00:11:32,213
Is there anybody else
we should talk to?

252
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:33,954
Um...

253
00:11:34,041 --> 00:11:37,000
What about Marie St. Claire?
She's on her way in here now.

254
00:11:37,087 --> 00:11:39,002
She's your girlfriend, right?

255
